Hi,

On Thu, 8 Jan 2004 13:27:03 -0800
"Glen Petrie" <glen.petrie@eitc.epson.com> wrote:
> The FSG-US group is continuing their discussion of a possible face-to-face
> meeting with FSG-Japan.   The FSG-US meeting members are unaware of a
> meeting at the New York Linux world but were still have an interest in
> having a face-to-face meeting with the FSG-Japan team.   Below are some of
> the options and questions about setting up a face-to-face meeting
> 
> There are two meeting options:
> 
> #1  (Best Option)  Joint face-to-face meeting with PWG, FSG-US and
> FSG-Japan.   The current meeting dates would be May 24th to May 28th.    The
> PWG is considering Japan or Vancouver, B.C. for the meeting.   Currently,
> Vancouver is the preferred choice since more people from North America will
> be able to attend and meetings were held in Japan in pervious years.
> 
> #2 Joint face-to-face meeting with FSG-US and FSG-Japan only.   End of April
> is the preferred meeting dates for this meeting by the FSG-US team. Location
> is open; either North America or Japan.
> 
> 
> 
> Purpose or possible agenda items:
> 
> 
> >FSG-Japan to provide detailed presentation to FSG-US(/PWG?) on the BI-DI
> and Vector Driver.
> 
> >FSG-US to provide detailed presentation to FSG-Japan(/PWG?) on
> Architecture, Job-Ticket, Programming-API (PAPI),  Image-Driver
> 
> >FSG-Japan/FSG-US to understand integration of API's under the (a) common
> Architecture
> 
> >FSG-Japan/FSG-US to discussion next steps (API, integration, testing, etc)
> for next 3-, 6-, 12- months
> 
> >FSG-Japan/FSG-US to prepare presentation for the FSG-Executive Committee
> 
> >FSG-Japan/FSG-US to prepare presentation for the PWG
> 
> 
> 
> Questions for the FSG-Japan and FSG-US:
> 
> Since this note is to determine interest by both teams, please respond to me
> or the mail distribution list of this note.   It is very important to
> determine who and where the possible meeting would be held before going
> further with meeting plans.
> 
> Would you attend a face-to-face meeting?
Yes, I'd like to attend the meeting.

> Which of the two meeting options (FSG-Japan/FSG-US only or
> FSG-Japan/FSG-US/PWG) is preferred by FSG-Japan?
Both are okay for me.

I think we should have a FSG/PWG joint meeting anyway to make a consensus
with each other, and if we can have a separate FSG only f2f meeting earlier,
I'd like to attend as mush as I can.

> Do you have a different suggested meeting option?
The last week of April may not work for many Japanese folks, because the
holiday week start from 29th until May 5th in Japan. So, I prefer another
day if we have a separate meeting.

> (FSG-Japan) Are you willing to travel to North America?
No problem.

> (FSG-US) Are you willing to travel to Japan?
> 
> Do you have any suggestions, changes or additions to the proposed agenda?
> 
> Any other comments?
